        "title": "Gauge Theory and the Standard Model",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Gauge theory is the framework in which the Standard Model is formulated. The central idea: the\nlaws of physics should be invariant under local (position-dependent) symmetry transformations.\nRequiring this invariance forces the existence of force-mediating fields. The symmetry group is\na Lie group; the forces are the curvature of a connection on a principal bundle."
